rem Digit Factorial Chains
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=74
rem Count starts below a limit with a
rem sixty-term digit factorial chain

use sequences
use graph
use io
use cli

option Limit integer = 1000000
option Terms integer = 60

rem Digit factorial sum f up to 2541000:
rem f(a * 1000 + b) = Head a + Pad b.
rem Pad counts leading zeros as 0! = 1;
rem Raw drops them for a lone b < 1000.
Fact = array shape 10
  1 1 2 6 24 120 720 5040 40320 362880
end
B = 0 to 999 array
Hi = B // 100
Mid = B // 10 mod 10
Lo = B mod 10
Pad = Fact Hi + Fact Mid + Fact Lo
Tens = (B at least 10) integer
Huns = (B at least 100) integer
Raw = Pad - (2 - Tens - Huns)
A = 0 to 2540 array
Low = A mod 1000
Thou = A // 1000
Wide = A at least 1000
Sum = Fact Thou + Pad Low
Head = Wide choose Sum (Raw Low)
Grid = Head Pad outer + copy
Grid 0 = Raw

rem Chains are paths of the successor
rem graph; lengths counts terms.
Flat = Grid reshape 2541000
Next = Flat drop 1
Lens = Next functional lengths
Short = Lens take (Limit - 1)
Answer = Short equal Terms count
Answer print
